    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d452">

                <pb facs="0810" n="682" sameAs="frus:frus1928v01/pg682"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">724.3415/244b: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        Argentina</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Bliss</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-12-09T18:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">December 9,
                                1928—6 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>62. The Department is sending the following telegram to the Legation in
                    Bolivia:</p>
                <p>[Here follows the text of telegram No. 31, December 9, 6 p.m., printed <hi
                        rendition="#italic">supra</hi>.]</p>
                <pb facs="0811" n="683" xml:id="pg683"/>
                <p>Please telegraph immediately your views as to whether any suggestion from the
                    Government of the United States to the Government of Bolivia along the line of
                    accepting the constitution of a Gondra commission would be misunderstood in
                    Argentina. Of course I do not wish to interfere with the Argentine mediation.
                    What action, if any, does the Government of Argentina contemplate in the present
                    situation?</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
